 *    - Update adminA's email and username and/or password to new, unique values (using PUT /discussionboard/admins/{id}).
 *    - Expect: 200 OK response with updated admin; fields changed, sensitive fields omitted.
 *    - Optionally test: audit log existence (if endpoint supported; omitted here due to lack of SDK).
 *    - Confirm by re-fetching the admin (not in SDK, unable to GET, but check via immediate return value).
 *
 * 3. Using non-privileged context (simulate as adminB):
 *    - Attempt update on adminA: expect 403 Forbidden or equivalent error (TestValidator.error).
