 *
 * Steps:
 * 1. Create a discussion board member (as the test user)
 * 2. Create notification preference(s) as that user, saving the created ID
 * 3. Fetch the notification preference by its ID and verify all returned fields (success path)
 * 4. Attempt to fetch a non-existent notification preference (random uuid) and expect failure (404 or equivalent)
 * 5. Create a second member (another user) and notification preference for them
 * 6. As the first user, attempt to fetch the other user's notification preference by ID, validate error/denial
 * 7. Call with an invalidly-formatted id (not a uuid) and expect validation/system error
 */
export async function test_api_discussionboard_test_retrieve_notification_preference_with_valid_and_invalid_id(
